        "diet": "Herbivore",
        "temperament": "Territorial",
        "wild": "Gigantopithecus fibrarator is a large, powerful ape that is usually quite passive unless approached too closely. It is territorial rather than outright aggressive, but its immense strength means any creature that triggers its defensive response is in serious danger. Its thick fur coat provides excellent insulation in cold environments.",
        "domesticated": "The Gigantopithecus must be passively tamed through careful hand-feeding without triggering its aggression. Once tamed, it is an imposing companion that can be equipped with hats and armor. A rider can engage in melee combat from its back. It can also carry passengers and toss them, and it excels at gathering fiber — its name literally means 'giant fiber-puller.'"
